version: 2.0.0
description: |
  Memory Steward CLI (A2, TD-2026-09-19-110) — the `paradigm memory` command
  group. A curation surface over Claude Code's NATIVE memory store
  (~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/). NEVER auto-deletes.

  Layers on A0 (premise-core #native-memory-scan: scanNativeMemory + path
  resolution) and A1 (core/memory: scoreEntry / clusterEntries / deriveFinding,
  pure). This dir adds the I/O + CLI.

  Findings surface as advisory remediations (.paradigm/remediations/, claimant
  'memory', severity 'advise') written DIRECTLY to the schema
  internal/active-remediations.ts reads — the remediation id is DERIVED from the
  entry path (rmd-mem-<hash>), so review is idempotent: a re-run overwrites (never
  duplicates) and preserves the original `created`, capping one active remediation
  per entry; resolved findings are archived to remediations/.archived/.

  Routing reuses existing typed homes: lore → core/lore/storage.recordLore; task
  → paradigm-mcp task-loader.createTask (relative-import precedent, same edge the
  `paradigm task` CLI already builds); habits → a DISABLED .habit stub in
  .paradigm/habits/ for human curation; decisions → a STUB decision YAML the user
  completes (NO cross-package lift of paradigm-mcp's decision-loader).

  All native-memory writes are path-safe (target must be inside the resolved
  memory dir) and fail-open (never crash). Output via cli-output.ts helpers.

  B2 adds the `sync` subcommand (advisory + strictly guarded, reworked
  2026-09-20): ADVISORY by default — prints a human report (size before/(projected)
  after, demotable leaf entries with prune/route hints, dedup candidates, unified
  diff, and — only with --projection — a projection preview) and writes NOTHING.
  Demotion is drastically narrowed (leaf ###+ only, provably graph-stale, no
  active-signal marker / recent date, no active-marked ancestor). Projection is OFF
  by default; opt in with --projection (compact, capped-at-8, deduped block).
  NOTE: the projection flag is `--projection`, NOT `--project`, because
  `-p, --project <path>` is the established project-root option on every memory
  subcommand. `--write` backs up then writes atomically. `--json` reports what
  would change (projectionEnabled + projectionItems).
components:
  memory-cli:
    description: The `paradigm memory` command group — review (batched digest with deterministic ids + idempotent advisory remediations + review stamp), apply-by-id subcommands prune / route / merge / pin, and sync (advisory report by default over a strictly-guarded lean rewrite; --projection opts into a compact/capped/deduped curated block; --write backs up + writes atomically; --json report). Path-safe, fail-open. Down-ranks pinned entries (.paradigm/memory-pins.json) and never surfaces the MEMORY.md index.
    type: command
    tags:
      - memory-steward
      - cli
      - curation
    path: index.ts
